  "body": "Depends on #300; this stacked PR isolates the next cover investigation while #300 completes integration.\n\nThe explicit run-index family leaves all-state coverage open. A natural proposed formal superset—strict real geometry, |x|<=n+1, |y|<=2, |sum(w)|<=1—is not forward closed. This PR provides one actual escaping edge for every n>=4, useful normalized eigenlength coordinates, exact Mojo replay and an independent calibration. It does not turn a formal overlap into a seed-reachable one.\n\n## Work shown\n\n### Assumptions and hypotheses\n\nUse the same minimal plus class-A line from #300, sigma=(x y^(n+1) x, c y^n x, x y^(n+1) c), n>=4. Overlaps use bottom-minus-top displacement, strict interior intersection and zero-based occurrence indices. The proof is a scoped written argument with coefficient-checked Mojo identities; independent human review remains pending.\n\n### Derivation / reduction\n\nLet h=1/(beta-1). The characteristic cubic gives P=h^3+(n+1)h^2+(n+1)h-1=0 and 0<h<1/5. Scaled tile lengths are (1+h+h^2,1,1+h), with every incidence-column eigenvector residual equal to P.\n\nV_n=(x,c,-n-1,n+4,-2) lies in the proposed rectangle. Its actual occurrence (0,3), whose bottom prefix is c y^2, gives W_n=(x,y,-n,n+3,-1), with coordinate sum 2. Scaled displacements reduce to h^3-2h and 1+h^2+h^3. The four strict margins are 1-2h+h^3, 1+3h+h^2-h^3, 2+h+h^2+h^3, and h(1-h)(1+h), all positive. Thus the cover fails uniformly, not merely at sampled parameters.\n\n### Evidence and replay\n\nSee docs/class-a-cover-obstruction-2026-10-21.md and evidence/class-a-cover-obstruction-2026-10-21/.\n\n- Canonical coefficient identities and strict real occurrence replay pass at n=4,8,18,64,256 with the reused lock-matched Mojo 1.1.0.dev2026090805 runtime.\n- Complete canonical seed graphs at n=4,18 omit both witnesses. The independently written Fraction-field oracle agrees on the edge, strict geometry and both finite nonmembership checks (275 and 835 seed vertices).\n- Focused accepted-scope, evidence-integrity and proof-bank regressions pass; provenance/governance passes and packet checksums verify.\n- The new dedicated workflow replays native tests, driver and independent calibration with locked Pixi. Fresh CI remains a separate requirement; the local minimal runtime receipt is not a fresh full-Pixi receipt.\n\n### Negative controls\n\nWrong bottom occurrence index, reversed displacement, changed child type, a damaged symbolic occurrence identity and input below the declared parameter range refuse. The independent oracle detects an altered occurrence index. Finite nonmembership is explicitly distinguished from uniform exclusion.\n\n### Non-claims / remaining gaps\n\nThis refutes the stated rectangular forward-cover reduction. It does not show a reachable child escape, nonhitting overlap, complete run-indexed cover, all-class-A/C BH, or universal #139. A valid cover must retain typed coordinate correlations or use a different invariant. Accepted class-D sources and receipts remain unchanged; #139 stays open. No governed claim is promoted.",
